                <pb facs="0839" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8952: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-14T17:00:00-05:00">March 14, 1941—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. Colonel Donovan reports from London that the Turkish Government has been
                    notified by Russia that the latter will not join with Germany in any attack on
                    Turkey if Turkey should defend itself against Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
